  "articleBody": "A felony drug conviction can cast a long shadow over your life, impacting far more than just your immediate freedom. Beyond potential prison time and hefty fines, you're looking at a range of collateral consequences that can severely limit your opportunities. For starters, your employment prospects can take a significant hit, as many employers are hesitant to hire individuals with felony records, especially for positions requiring professional licenses. Housing can become a major challenge, with landlords often performing background checks that reveal past convictions. You might also lose your right to vote, possess firearms, or even receive certain types of financial aid for education. Child custody arrangements could be affected, and your reputation within the community might suffer. The good news is that an experienced felony drug crime defense lawyer can often work to mitigate these impacts, sometimes by getting charges reduced or even dismissed. Exploring options like expungement or post-conviction relief with a professional like Angelo Reyes can help you reclaim your future, but acting quickly during your initial case is key.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
}